  "newPolicyDescription": "Review/quarantine an exact uncertain bulk intent, preserving its historical record. prepare_risk binds originalRequest and a replacementRequest with identical business effects; only preimage guards and explicit job association fields may change. inspect_risk presents known facts, missing evidence, caller reviewMemo and residual risks. Final risk approval is ONLY in the independent administrator workbench with fresh native owner verification; MCP cannot approve it. New human-risk-acceptance-v2 plans let the independent human administrator accept unknown historical and in-flight outcomes; no external migration receipt is required. After approval, create_replacement records managed original-job termination and creates/uploads the unique linked replacement. Historical outcome remains unknown. Creation never executes business writes; sealing and execution use normal bulk tools and immutable plan confirmation. Human acceptance is never a proof of non-execution or global legacy credential revocation; legacy policy plans retain their original requirements. Business ID/key values in results are opaque rda_ref_v1_ references. Reuse the complete reference in structured business-value arguments; the local wrapper restores its original BSON/EJSON type before validation. References are scoped to this MCP process and target database; never edit them, put them inside $oid, interpolate them into text/shell, or calculate chunkHash from them (omit chunkHash and use the agent's returned hash). After MCP restart, query again for fresh references.",
